issue (medium): 🟡 **Pressed scope filter cannot be removed** **(non-blocking)**

When `?scope=` already equals this scope, the button reads pressed and promises removal, but `nextMetadataFilterState` writes the same scope again, so the click does nothing.

Evidence: `packages/web/src/lib/filter-from-metadata.ts:288` (pressed tooltip promises removal) · `packages/web/src/components/lore/LessonDetailSheet.tsx:399` (writes next.scope unchanged)

```ts
if (target.kind === 'scope') {
  return {
    filters: filtersParamValue(current.filters, current.legacyTags, current.legacyOwner),
    scope: current.scope === target.scope ? null : target.scope,
  };
}
```

